  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the exact value of the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve $y=2{x}^{5}-8{x}^{4}+24{x}^{2}-16$ at the point where $x=3.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=2{x}^{5}-8{x}^{4}+24{x}^{2}-16.$ The slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is equal to ${f}^{′}(3).$ Computing the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{5}-8{x}^{4}+24{x}^{2}-16) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5{x}^{4}-8\\cdot 4{x}^{3}+24\\cdot 2x-0 \\\\  & =10{x}^{4}-32{x}^{3}+48x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate at $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(3) & =10({3}^{4})-32({3}^{3})+48(3) \\\\  & =810-864+144 \\\\  & =90.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at $x=3$ is\n\n$$\nm={f}^{′}(3)=90.\n$$",
